  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Urea-formaldehyde (UF) resin, one of the most important formaldehyde resin adhesives, is a polymeric condensation product of formaldehyde with urea, and being widely used for the&nbsp;manufacture of wood-based composite panels, such as plywood, particleboard, and fiberboard.</p><p>Urea <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>HCHO</mi></math> resin is used in manufacture of wood laminates.</p>",
